sequenceDiagram
    accTitle: SyncStream product projection and failure handling
    accDescr: Debezium publishes PostgreSQL changes to Kafka. Each independent consumer applies a product projection, retries eligible failures with bounded backoff, and attempts dead-letter publication if processing still fails. The current implementation commits offsets even if dead-letter publication fails.
    autonumber
    participant DB as PostgreSQL
    participant CDC as Debezium
    participant Kafka
    participant Consumer as Java Consumer
    participant Store as Redis or Elasticsearch
    participant DLQ as Dead-letter Topic

    DB-->>CDC: Committed row change via logical WAL
    CDC->>Kafka: Publish keyed product event
    Consumer->>Kafka: Poll subscribed product topic
    Kafka-->>Consumer: CDC event with source offset
    Consumer->>Store: Apply set, upsert or delete by ID
    alt Projection succeeds
        Store-->>Consumer: Operation completes
    else Projection fails
        Store-->>Consumer: Error
        Consumer->>Consumer: Classify error and retry within policy
        opt Still failing or not retryable
            Consumer->>DLQ: Attempt publish with error + source offset
            Note over Consumer,DLQ: Publication errors are logged
        end
    end
    Consumer->>Kafka: Commit current consumer offsets
    Note over Kafka,DLQ: Current code commits even if DLQ publish fails
